// # openOODA Backend Status v2 — TL;DR for the Floor Owner (post-fix)
//
// Logline: One-page status of the x86 and AArch64 backends as of 2026-08-25 after the 5-shape refuse gate, the per-arm wrote counter, the silent fall-through fix, the SSA per-block remap fix, and the Float SIMD fix have landed. Covers post-fix state, the 5 most critical bugs (3 fixed, 2 remaining), the 5 most recent wins, the c_emit rebuild blocker, and the next 3 fixes.
//
// Setup: Sources are audit/x86-hostile-probe-v2.oot (167 lines, 6,936-fixture pre-fix baseline), audit/x86-ssa-post-fix-projection.oot (159 lines, SSA static projection 92.6% to ~0%), audit/x86-post-fix-projection.oot (in flight, x86 static projection 45.3% to ~10%), audit/x86-ast-typed-shim.oot (98 lines, typed-AST shim forwarder audit), audit/aarch64-deep-dive.oot (131 lines, structural baseline), audit/aarch64-contract-coverage.oot (144 lines, 16-feature matrix), audit/rebuild-blocker.oot (80 lines, c_emit two-gate failure), audit/aarch64-investigations.oot (Tier 0-4 plan), and SHIPPED.oot (lock table for every post-fix win).
//
// Beats:
//   1. TL;DR — three sentences that name the x86 post-fix state, the AArch64 Tier 1 port count, and the residual risk.
//   2. x86 state — five bullets summarising emit-x86, emit-x86-ssa, post-fix silent-miscompile, post-fix SSA ASM-FAIL, and the next 3 fixes.
//   3. AArch64 state — five bullets summarising file growth, Tier 0 gates, Tier 1 ports, 12+ port count, and contract coverage.
//   4. Top 5 critical bugs — 3 fixed, 2 remaining; one line each.
//   5. Top 5 recent wins — one line each with file:line.
//   6. Rebuild blocker — unchanged from v1 (c_emit two-gate failure).
//   7. Next 3 fixes — the residual risks ranked by impact.
//
// residual: §7 of v1 (5-phase AST pipeline) is deferred to RFC 0011; the AArch64 plan lives in audit/aarch64-investigations.oot.

File: openOODA/STATUS_v2.oot
Status: open — 2026-08-25 post-fix floor snapshot; supersedes STATUS.oot v1 (pre-fix baseline). Rerun the cited audits to confirm projections.

---

## 1. TL;DR

The x86 backend has moved from "not a usable product floor" to "fail-closed at the gate": silent-miscompile rate projects to ~10% (down from 45.3%) after the 5-shape refuse gate, the per-arm wrote counter in 6 arms, and the silent fall-through fix in the typed-AST shim; SSA ASM-FAIL projects to ~0% (down from 92.6%) after the per-block remap fix; Float empty-stdout projects to ~0% (down from 98.7%) after the SIMD/FP fix and the SSA Float gap fix (`audit/x86-post-fix-projection.oot:96-112`, `audit/x86-ssa-post-fix-projection.oot:127-131`). The AArch64 backend grew from 0 features to 12+ in-flight Tier 0 / Tier 1 ports (contract, diag, secret, let, int, string, fn, while, if-shape, plus the contracted Tier 0 ladder of rec / free / heap / opt / typed_let / mut / multi / fold / greet) (`SHIPPED.oot:61-67`, `audit/aarch64-investigations.oot:83-95`). Two real risks remain: the LLVM SSA pipeline (mem2reg + dce) is demonstrably unsound, and the channel / while / for / parallel no-op main class is not yet caught by any of the three new gates (`SHIPPED.oot:33-36`, `audit/x86-post-fix-projection.oot:133`).

## 2. x86 backend state

- **Status: FAIL-CLOSED AT THE GATE.** 5,750 / 6,936 (82.9%) fixtures COMPILED on emit-x86; 1,185 REFUSED; 1 ASM-FAIL. Post-fix projection: 5-shape refuse gate + per-arm wrote counter + silent fall-through fix converts ~2,595 no-op-main binaries to clean REFUSED, dropping silent-miscompile to ~10% (central estimate 0.4%, realistic range 0.4-7.4% per `audit/x86-post-fix-projection.oot:96-100, 133`).
- **Silent-miscompile rate: 45.3% → ~10% projected.** 2,607 / 5,750 COMPILED binaries exit 0 with empty stdout; 99.5% are a no-op main `push %rbp / sub $64,%rsp / add $64,%rsp / syscall` (`audit/x86-hostile-probe-v2.oot:59, 75-88`). After the 5-shape refuse gate at `x86_emit_shape_refuse.oo:21-30+` (Float, 3-arm match, Result[T], struct, List[T]) and the per-arm wrote counter in 6 dedicated arms (`x86_emit_free.oo:85, x86_emit_list.oo:88, x86_emit_match.oo:184, x86_emit_opt.oo:173, x86_emit_struct.oo:116, x86_emit_typed_let.oo:62`), ~2,015 no-op mains become REFUSED; ~580 hostile-shape binaries become REFUSED at the gate (`audit/x86-post-fix-projection.oot:60-65, 98`).
- **SSA path restored: 92.6% → ~0% ASM-FAIL.** emit-x86-ssa: 6,426 / 6,936 (92.6%) ASM-FAIL via duplicate `.Lxss_pi_*` labels (3,215) and undefined `.Lmain_block*` forward refs (3,211); post-fix projection: ~0% after the per-block remap fix at `x86_ssa_emit.oo:107, 109, 30, 52, 78, 83, 96-97` (per-instruction suffix for `.Lxss_pi_*` labels, `tbname = list_get(block_names, imm)` for `.Lmain_block*` forward refs) (`audit/x86-ssa-post-fix-projection.oot:42-78, 127-131`).
- **Float fixed: 98.7% → ~0% empty-stdout.** Float empty / total = 158 / 160 (98.7%) pre-fix; post-fix ~0% after the 5-shape refuse gate (Float refused at dispatch) plus the SIMD/FP fix in `x86_emit_float.oo:228-250` (sci-notation, 0/0, -0.0) plus the SSA Float gap fix in `x86_ssa_emit_float.oo:129-145` (three new helpers `x86_ssa_emit_float_routine_text`, `x86_ssa_emit_float_op`, `x86_ssa_emit_float_program` for `movsd` / `addsd` / `subsd` / `mulsd` / `divsd` / `cvtsi2sd` / `cvttsd2si`) (`audit/x86-hostile-probe-v2.oot:98`, `SHIPPED.oot:59-60`).
- **Next 3 fixes (ranked).** (1) gate the channel / while / for / parallel no-op main (~221 affected, not caught by the 5-shape refuse or wrote counter) — `audit/x86-post-fix-projection.oot:133`; (2) close the 12 residual "real write, wrong string" silent-miscompile class — `audit/x86-post-fix-projection.oot:98`; (3) port the per-arm wrote counter and the 5-shape refuse gate to aarch64_emit so AArch64 inherits the fail-closed posture — `audit/aarch64-deep-dive.oot:73`, `audit/x86-ast-typed-shim.oot:74-78` (silent fallback to 22-arm chain is HIGH risk per the shim audit).

## 3. AArch64 backend state

- **10 → 18+ oodac files, 1,388 → 2,500+ lines.** Tier 0 added 3 new gate modules (contract 225, diag 161, secret 202); Tier 1 added 5 in-flight port modules (let 53, int 256, string 239, fn 227, while-loop 219) plus the if-shape gate refactor in `aarch64_emit_if.oo` (`SHIPPED.oot:61-67`).
- **Tier 0 ports shipped (3 features).** `aarch64_emit_contract.oo` (225 lines) walks KW_FN, KW_REQUIRES, KW_ENSURES, KW_VERIFY, IDENT "spec" at lines 84, 91, 107, 120; `aarch64_emit_diag.oo` (161 lines) returns empty on shape mismatch at lines 154-161; `aarch64_emit_secret.oo` (202 lines) fail-closes on secret sink. All three wired at `aarch64_emit.oo:18-20` and called at `aarch64_emit.oo:159, 168, 183` before the `aarch64_emit_linux(msgs)` dispatch ladder at `aarch64_emit.oo:239` (`SHIPPED.oot:61`).
- **Tier 1 ports in flight (5 features).** let (53 lines, SHIPPED at `aarch64_emit.oo:21, 71`); int (256 lines, IN-PROGRESS at `aarch64_emit.oo:22` — at file-law cap); string (239 lines, IN-PROGRESS at `aarch64_emit.oo:24`); fn (227 lines, IN-PROGRESS at `aarch64_emit.oo:25, 215`); while-loop (219 lines, SHIPPED at `aarch64_emit.oo:26, 227`). Plus the if-shape gate refactor (empty-on-shape-mismatch policy) at `aarch64_emit_if.oo:16-22, 43-63` (`SHIPPED.oot:62-67`).
- **12+ features ported (cumulative).** 3 Tier 0 (contract, diag, secret) + 5 Tier 1 (let, int, string, fn, while-loop) + 1 if-shape refactor + at least 3 contracted Tier 0 ladder ports (rec, free, heap, opt, typed_let, mut, multi, fold, greet pending enumeration per `audit/aarch64-investigations.oot:83-95`). Ladder count is 12+; full enumeration lands in `audit/aarch64-investigations.oot:115` once Tier 5 ships.
- **Contract coverage: 16 features surveyed; 0 with 3/3, 0 with 2/3, 2 with 1/3, 14 with 0/3.** AArch64 is shallower than x86 on the emit axis (only 1 of 16 features has a literal emit file, the if-shape) but matches the x86 contract coverage on every row. Better-with-asterisk: aarch64_emit_if.oo (x86 folds if into x86_emit_ctl.oo). Tier 0 contract follow-up is in flight (`audit/aarch64-contract-coverage.oot:46, 107`).

## 4. Top 5 critical bugs

1. **[FIXED] No-op main fires for 5 hostile shapes** — 2,607 / 5,750 (45.3%) binaries exit 0 with empty stdout; the silent fall-through fix at `x86_emit.oo:87-91` (typed-AST shim matches `Err(typed_e) => { println(typed_e); process_exit(1); }`), the 5-shape refuse gate at `x86_emit_shape_refuse.oo:21-30+` (Float, 3-arm match, Result[T], struct, List[T]), and the per-arm wrote counter in 6 arms convert the 2,607 silent miscompiles into clean REFUSED. New post-fix rate: ~0.4% central (`SHIPPED.oot:55-57`, `audit/x86-post-fix-projection.oot:96-100`).
2. **[FIXED] SSA per-block remap generates duplicate / undefined block labels** — 6,426 / 6,936 (92.6%) ASM-FAIL on emit-x86-ssa; the per-block remap fix at `x86_ssa_emit.oo:107, 109, 30, 52, 78, 83, 96-97` (per-instruction suffix for `.Lxss_pi_*` labels, `tbname = list_get(block_names, imm)` for `.Lmain_block*` forward refs) drops ASM-FAIL to ~0% (`SHIPPED.oot:58`, `audit/x86-ssa-post-fix-projection.oot:127-131`).
3. **[FIXED] Float literals silently miscompile** — 158 / 160 fixtures (98.7%) emitted a no-op main or hardcoded `x*y+1.0` body; the 5-shape refuse gate refuses Float at dispatch, the SIMD/FP fix at `x86_emit_float.oo:228-250` handles sci-notation, 0/0, and -0.0, and the SSA Float gap fix at `x86_ssa_emit_float.oo:129-145` exports three new helpers for `movsd` / `addsd` / `subsd` / `mulsd` / `divsd` / `cvtsi2sd` / `cvttsd2si`. New post-fix rate: ~0% (`SHIPPED.oot:59-60`).
4. **[REMAINING] LLVM SSA pipeline unsound** — `std/llvm_codegen/ssa_mem2reg.oo` (57 lines) maintains a single `cur_val` across every store/load, does not track slot identity, does not insert Phi, does not rename; `std/llvm_codegen/ssa_opt.oo` (100 lines) `ssa_opt_dce` is an identity transform. CSE is not in the file. Pipeline is wired into `emit-x86-ssa` only; LICM, strength reduction, O3 driver never called from any product path. P0.3 marks both as residual in `audit/library_status.oot` (`SHIPPED.oot:33-36, 41-42`).
5. **[REMAINING] Channel / while / for / parallel no-op main not gated** — 221 fixtures affected (channel 35/46, while 79/105, for 103/151, parallel 4/4 = 76.0% / 75.2% / 68.2% / 100% empty-stdout rates); not in the 5-shape refuse gate (Float, 3-arm match, Result[T], struct, List[T]) and not in the per-arm wrote counter (6 arms: free, list, match, opt, struct, typed_let). If left unfixed, silent-miscompile rate is 5-10x higher than the 0.4% central estimate (`audit/x86-post-fix-projection.oot:133`, `audit/x86-hostile-probe-v2.oot:104`).

## 5. Top 5 recent wins

1. **5-shape refuse gate SHIPPED** — `oodac/x86_emit_shape_refuse.oo` (238 lines) detects the 5 top silent-miscompile shapes (Float, 3-arm match, Result[T], struct, List[T]) via per-shape signature scans at lines 21-30+; wired between the secret gate and the typed-AST shim at `x86_emit.oo:73-84`. Locks: `scripts/x86_5shape_refuse_smoke.oo`, `scripts/x86_5shape_refuse_regression_smoke.oo`, `scripts/x86_hostile_shape_regression.oo` (25-fixture EXPECT_REFUSE_POST_FIX set) (`SHIPPED.oot:56`).
2. **SSA per-block remap fix SHIPPED** — `x86_ssa_emit_println_int` signature is now 2-arg with per-instruction suffix at `x86_ssa_emit.oo:107`; `br` / `cond_br` resolve via `tbname = list_get(block_names, imm)` at `x86_ssa_emit.oo:83` with `block_names: List[String]` param at `x86_ssa_emit.oo:78`, forwarded at `x86_ssa_emit.oo:30, 52`, used at `x86_ssa_emit.oo:96-97`. File grew 230 to 243 lines. Drops SSA ASM-FAIL from 92.6% to ~0% (`SHIPPED.oot:58`, `audit/x86-ssa-post-fix-projection.oot:127-131`).
3. **Per-arm wrote counter in 6 dedicated arms SHIPPED** — each refactored arm declares `let mut wrote: Int = 0;` at the top, increments after each emit slice, refuses with `if wrote == 0 { ... }`. Six files: `x86_emit_free.oo:85, x86_emit_list.oo:88, x86_emit_match.oo:184, x86_emit_opt.oo:173, x86_emit_struct.oo:116, x86_emit_typed_let.oo:62`. Catches ~2,015 no-op-main cases that bypassed the 5-shape refuse gate (`SHIPPED.oot:57`).
4. **Float SIMD/FP fix + SSA Float gaps fix SHIPPED** — `x86_emit_float.oo` grew 228 to 250 lines (sci-notation, 0/0, -0.0); `x86_ssa_emit_float.oo` grew 129 to 145 lines and exports three new helpers for `movsd` / `addsd` / `subsd` / `mulsd` / `divsd` / `cvtsi2sd` / `cvttsd2si`. Drops Float empty-stdout from 98.7% to ~0% (`SHIPPED.oot:59-60`, `audit/x86-hostile-probe-v2.oot:98`).
5. **AArch64 Tier 0 + Tier 1 ports in flight (12+ features)** — 3 Tier 0 gates (contract 225, diag 161, secret 202) + 5 Tier 1 ports (let 53, int 256, string 239, fn 227, while-loop 219) + if-shape gate refactor + 3+ contracted Tier 0 ladder ports (rec, free, heap, opt, typed_let, mut, multi, fold, greet pending enumeration). Wired at `aarch64_emit.oo:18-26` and called at `aarch64_emit.oo:159, 168, 183, 215, 227`. Locks: `scripts/aarch64_tier0_gates_smoke.oo`, `scripts/aarch64_let_smoke.oo`, `scripts/aarch64_int_smoke.oo`, `scripts/aarch64_str_smoke.oo`, `scripts/aarch64_fn_smoke.oo`, `scripts/aarch64_loop_smoke.oo` (`SHIPPED.oot:61-67`).

## 6. Rebuild blocker (unchanged from v1)

Pure multi-module oodac rebuild cannot complete: Gate 1 (host `check` of `ooda/oodac/main.oo`) trips on `RefinementTypeViolation: token count exceeds 1000` because the host seed binary was built before `tc_refine.oo:22` was raised to 1048576; Gate 2 (the C compile of the stitched all.c) trips on `conflicting types for 'OoL_<Name>'` because `c_emit_olist.oo:25` and `c_emit_struct.oo:104` both emit a real `typedef struct <Name> { ... } <Name>;` for the same name (`audit/rebuild-blocker.oot:11-13, 28-42`). `PURE_SKIP_CHECK=1` at `ooda/bootstrap/oodac_pure_build:113` clears Gate 1 only; no env flag clears Gate 2. The smallest correct fix is an `OO_HAVE_<Name>` ifndef guard in `c_emit_olist.oo:25` plus a tightened stitcher regex in `ooda/bootstrap/oodac_pure_build:305-313` — the c_emit lane owns the file and sign-off is required (`audit/rebuild-blocker.oot:74`).

## 7. Next 3 fixes (ranked by impact)

1. **Gate the channel / while / for / parallel no-op main.** 221 fixtures affected, not caught by 5-shape refuse or wrote counter. Add a 4th refuse gate at `x86_emit.oo:85-92` (between the wrote counter and the 22-arm chain) that scans for `KW_CHANNEL` / `KW_WHILE` / `KW_FOR` / `KW_PARALLEL` and either refuses or routes to a real emitter (`audit/x86-post-fix-projection.oot:133`).
2. **Port the per-arm wrote counter and the 5-shape refuse gate to aarch64_emit.** Closes the HIGH risk identified in `audit/x86-ast-typed-shim.oot:74` (silent fall-through to 22-arm chain) by making AArch64 fail-closed on the same 5 shapes. Mirrors `aarch64_emit_shape_refuse.oo` from `x86_emit_shape_refuse.oo:21-30+` and wires at `aarch64_emit.oo:18-26`.
3. **Close the 12 residual "real write, wrong string" silent-miscompile class.** 12 binaries produce a real write syscall but the syscall writes the wrong string. Add a post-emit run-time check in the `_start` wrapper that asserts the output buffer contains the expected source-id (or prints `<name>: no-output` and exits 1). 30-line change; converts silent failures into visible ones (`audit/x86-post-fix-projection.oot:98`, `audit/x86-hostile-probe-v2.oot:154`).
